Manage Energy, Find Safe Food, Prepare Food, And Support Long-Term Survival

Food provides:

energy for movement;

body heat;

recovery;

physical performance;

mental function.

However, food is usually not the first emergency priority.

In many wilderness situations, survival priorities begin with:

immediate safety;

shelter;

water;

medical needs.

Food becomes increasingly important as the situation extends.

The survival food system is:

MANAGE ENERGY

-

USE AVAILABLE RESOURCES

-

IDENTIFY SAFE FOOD

-

PREPARE CORRECTLY

=

SURVIVAL NUTRITION

The Survival Food Principle

The most common food mistake in survival is spending more energy finding food than the food provides.

A good survival food strategy focuses on:

high energy return;

low risk;

reliable sources;

efficient preparation.

high energy return;

low risk;

reliable sources;

efficient preparation.

