National Park Service guidance recommends carrying navigation tools and knowing how to use them as part of wilderness preparation.

Overview

Prevent a navigation mistake from becoming a larger survival emergency.

S --- Stop

Stop moving.

Avoid making the situation worse.

T --- Think

Ask:

Where was my last known location?

When was I last certain of my position?

What direction was I traveling?

What resources do I have?

O --- Observe

Check:

terrain;

weather;

water;

shelter options;

landmarks;

possible signals.

P --- Plan

Choose the safest action:

remain in place;

return along a known route;

move toward a known location;

signal for help.

If lost or disoriented, staying calm and attempting to determine location before moving is a key wilderness safety principle.

